    <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How does Meta + Instagram Ads work for a jewelry brand in Bengaluru?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Meta Ads (Facebook + Instagram + Reels) is your #1 paid channel for a jewelry brand in Bengaluru, typically 40-50% of ad spend. Core stack: (1) Advantage+ Shopping (AAS) — Meta's automated campaign, feeds catalog + creative + audience signals, drives 3-6x ROAS. (2) Catalog Sales dynamic product ads for retargeting + prospecting. (3) Reels + short video (35-45% of creative mix, highest algorithmic priority). (4) Creator UGC content whitelisted via Meta Branded Content Partner. (5) WhatsApp CTWA (Click-to-WhatsApp) ads. (6) Meta CAPI (Conversion API) recovers 15-30% attribution lost to iOS 14+. (7) LTV-weighted value-based bidding. In Bengaluru, Bengaluru buyer LTV/CAC-driven + tech-savvy + Shopify + headless architecture + high subscription adoption"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What CPL should we expect on Meta Ads for a jewelry brand in Bengaluru?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In INR: Rs 200-2,500 (India), AED 15-200 (GCC), £8-120 (UK) depending on tier. Range depends on sub-vertical + AOV + creative quality + audience quality + brand-recall level. Peak season (Wedding + Akshaya Tritiya + Dhanteras + Diwali (India), Ramadan + Eid + Dubai Shopping Festival (GCC), Christmas + Valentine's Day + Mother's Day (UK)) CPL rises 30-60% but conversion rate + AOV lifts 30-50% — net ROAS stays flat or improves. Off-peak CPL 20-30% lower + higher share of experimental testing budget. Creator UGC in retargeting drops CPL 30-50% vs studio content. Effective cost per acquired customer = CPL / conversion rate. In Bengaluru, India's tech + startup capital + VC-backed D2C founders + SaaS + fintech + product/engineering leaders + design + tech-native buyer"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What creative velocity + format mix for Meta Ads for a jewelry brand?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Boutique tier: 4-8 creative units/week. Growth tier: 15-30/week. Enterprise tier: 30-80/week (fast-fashion + streetwear + high-drop-frequency categories). Below velocity, CPL climbs 25-50% within 60 days from creative fatigue. Format mix: Reels + short video 35-45% (highest engagement + Meta priority), carousel product + collection 20-25%, single image lifestyle 10-15%, creator UGC + testimonial 15-20% (highest CTR + lowest CPL on retargeting), static product with overlay 5-10%, long-form video (60-90 sec) 5%. For Jewelry in Bengaluru, video-first creative outperforms static 3-5x."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much monthly Meta ad budget should we spend?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In Bengaluru: Rs 2-18 lakh. Rule of thumb: 20-35% of monthly revenue during launch validation (first 6 months), 15-25% during scaling (month 6-24), 8-18% mature-brand (Rs 2+ crore/month revenue). Peak season (Wedding + Akshaya Tritiya + Dhanteras + Diwali (India), Ramadan + Eid + Dubai Shopping Festival (GCC), Christmas + Valentine's Day + Mother's Day (UK)) concentrates 40-60% of annual ad spend in 12-16 weeks. AOV context: India Rs 3,500-25,000 (fashion + gold-plated), Rs 20,000-1,50,000 (fine gold + diamond), Rs 1L-25L+ (bridal + solitaire), GCC AED 250-2,500 (fashion), AED 2,500-25,000 (fine + gold), AED 25,000-500,000+ (bridal), UK £150-1,500 (fashion + silver + gold-plated), £1,500-15,000 (fine gold + diamond), £5,000-100,000+ (bridal + engagement) — higher AOV supports higher CPL breakeven + higher absolute ad spend."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do we set up Meta CAPI (Conversion API) + attribution?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Meta Conversion API essential — server-side event tracking recovers 15-30% attribution lost to iOS 14+ tracking restrictions. Setup: (1) Server-side via Shopify + Meta integration OR (2) Segment/GTM Server-Side implementation OR (3) Direct CAPI Gateway integration. Weekly event match quality monitoring — target 8.5+/10 EMQ score. Combine with Google Enhanced Conversions + WhatsApp CTWA click tracking + Shopify order-level attribution + Triple Whale/Northbeam for full-stack attribution. Attribution recovery drives 20-40% more efficient scaling for Jewelry brands."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What Advantage+ Shopping best practices for a jewelry brand?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"(1) Complete catalog feed with Jewelry-specific attributes (colour + material + size + style + occasion + AOV tier). (2) 15-25+ creative assets — mix of static + video + creator UGC + carousel. (3) Audience signals: existing customer + LAL of subscribers + high-intent + interest-based. (4) Enable existing customer expansion + value-based bidding. (5) Weekly creative refresh — Jewelry categories with seasonal creative rotate every 3-4 weeks. (6) Segment PMax + AAS by margin tier + trend + seasonality via custom labels. (7) Exclude brand terms from AAS (protect direct brand-search ROAS)."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the role of Reels + short video in Meta Ads for jewelry?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Reels + short video (15-45 seconds) is the highest-priority format in 2026 Meta algorithm — 35-45% of paid creative mix. Winning Reels formats for Jewelry: (1) Trend-audio + hashtag-challenge creative, (2) Creator UGC unboxing + styling + review, (3) Product-showcase + demo (15-30 sec), (4) Behind-scenes + team + production content, (5) Before-after or transformation (where applicable), (6) Educational + tutorial + how-to. Reach 100K-10M+ per viral piece. Whitelist creator Reels via Meta Branded Content Partner for 30-50% CPL reduction."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does WhatsApp CTWA + Meta integration work?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Click-to-WhatsApp (CTWA) ads drive high-intent purchase conversation for Jewelry brands, especially higher-AOV segments. In Bengaluru, WhatsApp Cloud API (Interakt/AiSensy) handles: initial qualification + product recommendation + AOV upsell + booking confirmation + post-purchase follow-up. Response SLA: within 5 min business hours. Multilingual templates for India — English + Hindi + Marathi/Tamil/Bengali (India), English + Arabic + Hindi (GCC), English (UK primary). Conversion 20-40% on qualified WhatsApp leads. Attribution via CTWA click tracking + custom UTM + offline conversion upload."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the biggest Meta Ads mistakes for jewelry brands in Bengaluru?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"(1) Optimising for first-purchase CPA vs LTV (compresses long-term margin 20-40%). (2) Low creative velocity — fatigue drives CPL up 30-60% in 60-90 days. (3) No Meta CAPI (30% attribution loss vs pixel-only). (4) Weak catalog feed (missing category-specific attributes). (5) Same audience + creative across all sub-categories/AOV tiers (should segment). (6) No creator UGC in retargeting (studio content underperforms 20-40%). (7) English-only creative in Bengaluru — Bengaluru buyer LTV/CAC-driven + tech-savvy + Shopify + headless architecture + high subscription adoption. (8) Ignoring WhatsApp CTWA for high-AOV segments. (9) Weak landing pages killing paid conversion. (10) No peak-season concentration (Wedding + Akshaya Tritiya + Dhanteras + Diwali (India), Ramadan + Eid + Dubai Shopping Festival (GCC), Christmas + Valentine's Day + Mother's Day (UK))."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does LTV-weighted bidding work for a jewelry brand?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Traditional CPA optimisation targets first-purchase cost. LTV-weighted bidding targets long-term customer value — pays more upfront for customers with higher 12-24 month LTV. Setup: (1) Import LTV data to Meta via Value column in offline conversion upload OR CAPI value field, (2) Enable value-based bidding in AAS + catalog campaigns, (3) Set target cost per acquisition based on cohort LTV not first-purchase revenue, (4) Weekly LTV/CAC dashboard tracks subscription-cohort + repeat-buyer + upsell-buyer separately. For Jewelry brands: LTV context — Highest LTV of D2C categories — 5-year LTV Rs 25K-40L (India), AED 3K-500K+ (GCC), £2K-100K+ (UK). LTV-weighted bidding drives 25-50% more efficient scaling by month 6+."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do we track ROI for Meta Ads for a jewelry brand in Bengaluru?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Weekly KPIs: spend + ROAS + CAC + CPL + creative fatigue + LTV/CAC ratio + attribution health (CAPI event match quality). Monthly QBR: full P&L attribution + cohort LTV + subscription-cohort retention (if applicable) + creative + audience performance breakdown + next-month optimisation plan. Quarterly: cohort revenue attribution + LTV/CAC by cohort + creative refresh strategy + peak-season readiness. In Bengaluru with Bengaluru buyer LTV/CAC-driven + tech-savvy + Shopify + headless architecture + high subscription adoption, seasonal (Wedding + Akshaya Tritiya + Dhanteras + Diwali (India), Ramadan + Eid + Dubai Shopping Festival (GCC), Christmas + Valentine's Day + Mother's Day (UK)) reporting adds daily performance during peak windows."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does ITD manage Meta Ads for a jewelry brand in Bengaluru?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Full-stack execution: Advantage+ Shopping + Catalog Sales + Reels + creator UGC + WhatsApp CTWA + Meta CAPI + LTV-weighted bidding + creative production (in-house pod 15-30 units/week Growth-tier) + weekly performance review + monthly QBR. Reference brands: CaratLane, Bluestone, Melorra, Giva, Isharya, Fabelia, Mia by Tanishq (India); Damas, Malabar, Joyalukkas (GCC); Astley Clarke, Monica Vinader, Missoma (UK). Retainer Rs 90K-3.5 lakh/month + ad spend transparent pass-through (no markup). Free 30-min discovery call — we audit your Meta + benchmark against 3-5 competing Bengaluru Jewelry brands + share customised 90-day plan within 3 working days."}}]}</script>
